course: dictionary
lesson: 2729
title: Diplomats and tact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diplomat is a person who speaks for their country when they are in another country. Their job is to help the two governments talk to each other and agree on things.
explain: «China and Taiwan trade a lot with each other, and diplomats work every day to keep the peace.» The clues are trade, work every day and keep the peace. So a diplomat helps countries get on with each other without fighting.
explain: The second meaning is about people. Someone who is tactful knows what to say so that nobody gets upset. If you call a friend «a real diplomat», you mean they are good at calming arguments. To check, swap in a word like peacemaker and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A diplomat represents their country in another country.
fact: Diplomats help governments talk, agree and solve problems peacefully.
fact: Diplomats often work in embassies.
fact: «A born diplomat» means someone who is naturally good at not upsetting people.
fact: «Diplomatic» describes something done with care and tact, so it does not upset anyone.
exercise: «China and Taiwan trade a lot with each other, and diplomats work every day to keep the peace.» What is a diplomat's job in this sentence? | Teaching children to swim | Selling cars to other countries | *Helping countries keep the peace
exercise: Ella says her friend is «a real diplomat». What does diplomat mean here? | Someone who always starts arguments | *Someone good at calming arguments without upsetting people | A person who lives in a palace
exercise: «Ben knew exactly what to say, so nobody got upset.» What does this show about Ben? | He was asleep | *He was tactful | He was rude
test:
Find and copy one word from the sentence that means working with care so nobody gets upset. | diplomatic | embassy | trade | *tactful
What is a diplomat? | A person who fixes cars | *A person who represents their country in another country | A person who writes books about the sea | A person who runs a shop
exam:
Which word best describes someone who helps two governments agree, without upsetting either side? | Curt | Glum | *Diplomat | Barely
